{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1383256-lone-wolves-packless-garou","id":1383256,"title":"Lone Wolves / Packless Garou","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-22T17:57:15-07:00","id":1383256,"title":"Lone Wolves / Packless Garou","content":"I've recently started thinking about the role of packless Garou in Garou society and septs. While Garou are social, pack oriented creatures, they still have to have individuals who stay on their own for any number of reasons. They might attend caern moots and be considered part of a sept, or perhaps mostly stay by themselves and don't attend septs (at least not regularly). I am not talking about Ronin, the Bone Gnawer Rabble, or other dubious werewolves who aren't part of Garou society. These would be Garou who are members in good standing. It's just they aren't members of a pack, and haven't been for a long time (as opposed to Garou who are temporarily between packs).<br /> <br /> In Revised, we had a Bone Gnawer tribal Gift for a packless Gnawer to gain benefit of a pack totem for a pack for which he wasn't a member. I assume it was used by wandering lone Bone Gnawers (who perhaps wouldn't be allowed to officially join a pack, because he's a filthy Bone Gnawer presumably). (The Gift also went into detail about using it on a caern totem which is out of scope for this discussion).<br /> <br /> Silent Striders are generally depicted as being by themselves wandering between septs, and very often don't seem to have a pack.<br /> <br /> Stargazers too fit that same mold although for a different reason.<br /> <br /> And there are rules for Personal Totems, but I can't remember which books they are in. I think it is a Merit or Background. But it's something Garou who aren't in packs can use.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, there really isn't anything in the normal Renown Chart which indicates a packless Garou is punished. There is a statement about &quot;living alone, without one's pack, except for ritual reasons&quot; but that sounds more like a Garou neglecting his pack responsibilities as opposed to someone not being a member.<br /> <br /> So there seems to be some allowance for packless Garou. They might be thought as misfits, strange or eccentric, but they seem to be accepted.<br /> <br /> So how frequent do we think these packless Garou are? No doubt, they are more prevalent in certain tribes than others. Do you think they fulfill any special kind of roles? What are good ways an ST can utilize them in games? Have you ever played one yourself, perhaps in a solo player game with your ST?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T02:29:04-07:00","id":1383317,"title":"","content":"Well, they can be quest givers, they can provice a couter argument for the standpoint the elders of a sept give to the players, they can act as mentors and a lot of other stuff, I guess.<br /> <br /> I usually would use garou like that if I needed an NPC but wasn't willing to design a pack or believe that in the planned scene more then one character wouldn't make the scene work, but it was implausible for character not to have his pack with him, if he had one =&gt; so, packless garou it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T23:29:18-07:00","id":1383518,"title":"","content":"I've found the write up for Mouse in Tribebook: Bone Gnawers. It's under the totems section as 1 dot, and personal only. Interestingly, the totem is listed as a <i>gaffling</i> while pack totems are always referred to as jaggling avatars. It also makes the connection to the Great White Mouse and states that Mouse's survival depends on hiding from predators. It's powers are fairly weak, but as an option for the Totem background, a single Garou could spend more points in totem and make it a more powerful spirit.<br /> <br /> While this is not mentioned in the tribebook, I always remember the wording in the second edition corebook that Mouse was once a minor totem of Garou until the newly formed Bone Gnawers killed all the Garou children of Mouse, demoting it to even lesser status. Presumably Rat forced Mouse into its brood ever since. First edition corebook explicitly states that the Great White Mouse was once the pack totem of the BG pack that saved the Central Park caern, and that afterwards Mouse became the second totem of the caern. First edition also states that at one point the tribal Incarnas were once the totem of packs that became the totem of caerns and e ventually grew in power to become a tribal incarna. So there is an implied backstory that the Mouse totem has begun a slow climb back in power ever since that BG pack in New York saved the Central Park caern. It's enough that Mouse can now be a personal totem, if not a pack totem.<br /> <br /> That Mouse is now mentioned as a personal totem among the Bone Gnawers, it implies that at least in the modern day there are a lot of lone Bone Gnawers who make use of the totem. So that tribe likely has the highest number of packless Garou, And that for these Garou, the Sept of the Green is probably a good place to make a pilgrimage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T05:26:47-07:00","id":1383574,"title":"","content":"That feels like... reading a lot into one Totem, also a lot that's specific to early books and not really referenced or reflected in later ones. Esp. since it's well established in the lore now that Totem spirits that are avatars of the same larger spirit don't always manifest the same way. There's three different versions of Sphinx in Revised as an example. Mouse as a personal Totem and Great White Mouse can both exist as separate avatars of Mouse.<br /> <br /> Personal Totems are in W20 core for whatever that's worth, and is detailed in the Totem Background write up as a sidebar. W20 opted to get rid of the mechanical hurdles previous editions had and just have it as something some Garou do.<br /> <br /> The two biggest groups of packless Garou (baring the groups you cut out already) are Cliaths still looking for a permanent pack (the books generally present it that many Garou go through a few temporary pack before landing their permanent one so they can contribute in the meantime), and older Garou that have settled into various positions usually within a Sept, after their packs have died in battle and so on.<br /> <br /> The Cliaths aren't given much spotlight, because few people play the game where the PCs go through that. That said they can be useful as temporary additions to the PC pack if they have something they're lacking (the Theurge focused on spirit negotiations, so they don't have a healer), and there are Rites to help make it work. The older ones are (and there's plenty of examples in the books) are NPCs and used for any number of ST purposes. Proven Garou that opt to not join a pack again, and instead focus on duties to more sedentary roles are still valuable to the nation and useful for structuring game-play.<br /> <br /> So, I'd say most Septs have some un-packed Garou around, and most would have at least one or two Athro or Elder Garou that have taken up a position (either a standard Sept position, or a Tribal one) and thrown themselves into that role over finding a pack (esp. in smaller Septs where they might be the only Garou of that Rank and might feel it would mess with pack dynamics to have an Elder pack with a bunch of Fosterns).<br /> <br /> I would contest the idea that some Tribes are more prone to it than others. The Gnawers just have more numbers than the others, so most things are more numerous among them. The Striders are generally stated as being in packs, but leave for personal missions and come back (nomads don't keep moving from place to place, they generally follow a cycle). The Stargazers form might not always join packs, but they have the Beast Courts to fill that niche with as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T17:04:10-07:00","id":1383689,"title":"","content":"There would certainly be Garou between packs that qualify. The Garou in that case likely want to be part of a pack, so I imagine they aren't packless for long. They either find an existing pack at the sept they can join, form their own with like Garou, or leave the sept to find better opportunities at other septs. I don't think Garou would be packless for long. Maybe less than 6 months, or a year at most. I imagine for many such Garou, it's like trying to find a job - they'll accept anything that fits if it means getting back to work sooner rather than waiting for that perfect pack.<br /> <br /> I hadn't considered sept leaders would be packless. In many games I've seen, the sept leaders are often part of the same &quot;sept management&quot; pack. Or if they're not, each of the leaders have their own packs (with some leaders being in the same pack as others). I think packless leaders would be rare. First, it sets a bad example to the other Garou. Second, leaders need political support from the other members of the sept, and one's packmates are a strong source of such support. But I could see them in rare circumstances such as a treasured elder outliving his pack and being allowed to continue his sept duties for a little while. But I think such packless Garou would be poltiically isolated and be set up for challenges by more ambitious Garou who have more solid backing. Your example would also fit - a lone elder ranked Garou at a small caern with lots of low ranking Garou. But I think even in that case, such a leader would benefit by calling in favors from a friend elsewhere to come join him in a pack to help him lead the caern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T03:56:22-07:00","id":1383747,"title":"","content":"That's kind of a rosy picture compared to the books. The majority of Caerns are weaker ones, and thus have less Garou defending them compared to the big Rank 5 Caerns that are so precious. The Garou also simply aren't numerous enough to ensure every Caern has a full pack leading it. Smaller Caerns with ten or so Sept members aren't going to be attractive to ambitious Garou, aren't going to be easy to call in favors for (since that means pulling a skill and proven Garou away from a more potent Caern and duty to that is going to be an issue), and a Cliath pack + a mid-ranking Pack and... you're already light on Garou to even form a leadership pack. There's also things like smaller/weaker Caerns meaning less/lower range Moon Bridges to call for help with.<br /> <br /> These sorts of Caerns are supposed to be the most numerous, but in general they're also the least used in play because of how limited they are. All the big cool stuff is happening at the big Caerns, and the Septs built around them make it easier to justify a wider range of Tribes, and have enough Garou to cover all the essentials so young packs (aka the PCs) can go out on quests without leaving the Sept crippled in operations, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T19:38:39-07:00","id":1384077,"title":"","content":"If you are talking about really small caerns, I don't see there being enough Garou at any one age cohort to lead to a situation where there are lots of young ranking Garou and only one elder. What's the likelihood of having a full pack's worth of young Garou be produced by nearby kinfolk or Garou? So I think it'd be very rare to see something like 1 Elder and 6 Cliath. More likely 1 Elder, 1 Ahtro, 2 Adren, 2 Fostern, and 1 Cliath let's say. It'd be a mix of some kind. I think many of those rank 1 caerns would have some kind of mix like that, so there could be one caern leadership pack, and a younger pack that would go out and do stuff. You don't need that many Garou to do that. 8 Garou would be enough to fill two packs. And it doesn't need to be a &quot;full pack&quot; leading the sept. Not just one Garou. Even a pack of two or three is still a pack.<br /> <br /> And as for the times when your example does hold, I do think there would be some Garou who would be willing to move and join up to lead a caern. There's a time when Garou switch to being young, active warriors to aging teachers and mentors. And the Renown Chart rewards Honor and Wisdom to Garou who take a more active sept leadership role. For some Garou who are ambitious, but limited in their ambitions, it would be attractive to leave a larger sept where there's lots of competition for those leadership roles to go to a smaller caern in need and get the prestige of being called Master of the Rite, Gatekeeper, or some other leadership role which will give them the Renown they need to advance to that next rank.<br /> <br /> So I don't think it's necessarily that I am painting a rosy picture. I do think there's real reason why a Garou might leave to help out a smaller caern and help out a lone higher ranked Garou. Hell, it might even be a rank challenge for some Garou, or part of an apprenticeship before going back to a larger caern and going out for a position there. (I don't know if you are ready yet to be Rite Master at our caern. Why don't you head out to that Rank 1 Caern and help out Lightbringer with his sept duties there? It's just him and a pack of young Garou. It'll give you some experience at being a Master of Rite, and you'll be more likely to be accepted as our Master of Rite when you come back. A few years there will help him and you both out.)<br /> <br /> I do think your example would happen some of the time. But I don't think it'll be the norm. Not unheard of, but not typical.<br /> <br /> As for what happens to all those rank one caerns and how they manage to survive, be abandoned, or lost to the enemy, I think it would deserve its own thread. It would be a big topic and generate a lot of ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}